From: pseudo <cdodge@pseudoseed.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:52:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] [Spec 250][Phase: phase_8] docs: re-shoot both phases
 after the label and marker changes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed on screen: the terminal excerpt is captioned, the row marker is a
gavel plus the gate name instead of 'Gate: <name>', and a gated ARCHITECT now
keeps its role caption, its gate and its title on the same row.

One clip remains and is deliberate: at 1440 the sidebar is ~232px, and a gated
architect whose gate name is 15 characters shows 'Archit…' for the role caption.
The gate name and the thread title are both intact — an architect at a gate is
the row a human most needs to find, so the gate keeps its full name and the
caption spends the last few pixels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
